course: dictionary
lesson: 7272
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Pin is a good example. It can be a thing (a noun) or an action (a verb).
explain: «A 4-digit PIN has 10,000 possible codes» uses pin as a secret number, not a piece of metal. The words «codes» and «keypad» are the clues. Ask yourself: what word would fit here?
explain: «He pins the driver down with his elbow» uses pin as a verb meaning to hold someone so they cannot move. Try swapping in «fasten» and the sentence stops making sense, so this is a different meaning.
fact: A pin is a short, thin, sharp piece of metal with a round head, used to hold cloth or paper together.
fact: A pin can also be a small badge, or a PIN, which is a secret number used with a bank card or phone.
fact: To pin something means to fasten it with a pin.
fact: To pin someone down means to hold them so they cannot move.
exercise: «Keep pins and needles away from babies.» What is a pin in this sentence? | *A short, thin, sharp piece of metal | A small piece of cloth | A kind of bird | A secret number
exercise: «Never share your PIN or passwords.» What does PIN mean here? | To fasten something | A small badge | *A secret number used with a bank card or phone | A sharp needle for sewing
exercise: Ella says, «She pinned the poster to the wall.» What does pinned mean? | Held someone so they could not move | Shouted loudly | Hid under a blanket | *Fastened with a pin
test: «Put the pin back in the pin cushion.» Which meaning of pin is used? | A noun meaning a secret number | A verb meaning to fasten | A verb meaning to hold someone still | *A noun meaning a short, thin, sharp piece of metal
test: «The police pinned the thief against the wall until help came.» What does pinned mean? | A small badge | To fasten with a pin | A secret number | *To hold someone so they cannot move
exam: «He wore a pin on his jacket.» What is a pin in this sentence? | To fasten something | A secret number | *A small badge | To hold someone still
